# Lake build output and fetched dependencies. Everything here is derived from
# tracked sources plus the pinned toolchain, so it is reproducible rather than
# archival.
/.lake/
**/*.olean
**/*.ilean
**/*.trace
**/*.hash

# `lean-toolchain` and `lake-manifest.json` are NOT ignored. SPEC section 4 pins
# the exact Lean commit and every package revision, and the release gate
# recomputes those identities from the checked-in files. Ignoring either would
# make offline verification trust the environment instead of the tree.

# `artifacts/` is NOT ignored. SPEC section 5 requires the committed
# `wasm-gemm-gnaf.wasm`, the Atlas seal, and the proof manifest to be in the
# tree; `artifact-check` compares every committed byte against
# `Release.committedArtifactBytes`.

# `CONFORMANCE.md` is NOT ignored. It is generated from `model/claims.json`, and
# `reproducible.yml` asserts it is byte-clean after regeneration -- which
# requires it to be tracked.

# Scratch written by the gate and the axiom auditor. Both delete their probe on
# the success path; these entries cover an interrupted run.
/.gate_axioms.lean
/.axioms_probe.lean

# Scratch Lean. Anything under `WasmGemmGnaf/` that belongs to no SPEC section 5
# layer is rejected by `just root-check` rather than ignored here -- a scratch
# module in the proof path is a defect to surface, not to hide.
/scratch/
/tmp/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Python bytecode from the gate tools.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
